From: waydroid-nvidia
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: handle RGB565 read-back and partial buffer cleanup

Play Store detail previews produce RGB565 software-decoder buffers. The
wl_shm fallback rejected format 4 and its partial buffer destructor called
wl_buffer_destroy(nullptr), crashing the whole composer. EGL read-back
already converts the source into 32-bit BGRA, so use XRGB8888 for RGB565.
Only destroy resources that were actually acquired, including mmap failure.

Source: waydroid-nvidia; reproduced 2026-11-18 on Play Store details
License: MIT (upstream Waydroid hwcomposer files)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp b/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp
index 2890ad6..20938bc 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@ namespace {
         uint32_t fmt;
 
         switch (hal_format) {
+            // EGL read-back produces 32-bit BGRA even for a 16-bit source.
+            case HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGB_565:
             case HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGBX_8888:
                 fmt = WL_SHM_FORMAT_XRGB8888;
                 break;
diff --git a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
index b035700..30a8f57 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
@@ -110,9 +110,9 @@ struct buffer;
 buffer::~buffer() {
     if (prime)
         prime_release_source(prime_source);   /* wl_buffer belongs to the copy-target pool */
-    else
+    else if (wl_buffer)
         wl_buffer_destroy(wl_buffer);
-    if (isShm)
+    if (isShm && shm_data && shm_data != MAP_FAILED)
         munmap(shm_data, size);
 }
 
